  "source": "[P \\.xor./ Q]\nStates:\nwhen: P, Q is \\\\statement\nthat: (P \\.or./ Q) \\.and./ \\not{P \\.and./ Q}\nDocumented:\n. written: \"P+? \\text{ xor } Q+?\"\n. description: \"The exclusive disjunction of $P$ and $Q$. It holds when $P$ or\n                $Q$ holds but *not* both, and is defined here as $(P \\text{ or }\n                Q) \\text{ and } \\neg(P \\text{ and } Q)$ -- inclusive *or* with\n                the both-true case removed.\"\nId: \"1c7bc638-0db8-416f-a0d0-f5c0d7d92842\"",
